<section aria-labelledby="eras-h">
  <h2 id="eras-h">What changed in 2025–2026</h2>
  <p class="sub">Two patterns run through almost everything in this scan. They are the spine of the 2027 series.</p>
  <div class="eras">
    <div class="era">
      <span class="tag">Era 01</span>
      <h3>The custom operator family era</h3>
      <p>RayTK was the first custom operator family, inspiring Josef Pelz's T3D and the custom families that followed. T3D grew into TDXFam, and TDXFam became the substrate for a wave of new families: GSOPs (Gaussian splats), L2D (2D lighting), MOPs (modular synthesis), POPX, AML (Apple ML), and Function Store's FNS family. Builders are no longer shipping single .tox files — they are shipping operator families with installers, versioning, and docs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="era">
      <span class="tag">Era 02</span>
      <h3>The MCP era</h3>
      <p>At least five distinct TouchDesigner MCP servers exist as of October 2026 — TwoZero, Embody's Envoy, 8beeeaaat's touchdesigner-mcp, Pantani's tdmcp / MindDesigner, and Derivative's own official TDMCP, launched September–October 2026 — plus a same-named package on PyPI. AI agents can now build networks directly inside TouchDesigner.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

