<section aria-labelledby="cat-h" style="padding-top:18px">
  <h2 id="cat-h">The catalogue</h2>
  <p class="sub">Price and licence are stated only where a public page exposed them. Where Patreon did not expose a tier table, the entry says so — those amounts are marked <span class="badge b-unv">Unverified</span> and should be checked on the tier page before quoting them anywhere.</p>
  <div class="grid" id="grid"></div>
  <div class="noresults" id="noresults">No entries match that filter. Clear the search or pick “All.”</div>

  <h3 style="margin-top:26px">Also spotted — not full entries</h3>
  <ul class="plain" style="list-style:none;margin:0">
    <li><strong>L2D operator family</strong> — TDXFam-built family for real-time 2D lighting (Monte Carlo GI, Radiance Cascades, Direct renderers; Windows + Mac). Author name not exposed on the fetched posts — unverified. <a href="https://www.patreon.com/posts/tox-l2d-operator-155965844">Patreon post</a></li>
    <li><strong>TD-ML</strong> — ML toolkit for CHOPs (MLP/LSTM, VAE, UMAP; scikit-learn / PyTorch), beta/experimental, by “bi.os” / Joel per forum replies. <a href="https://derivative.ca/community-post/asset/td-ml-v02-machine-learning-toolkit-touchdesigner/73917">Derivative Community post</a></li>
    <li><strong>touchdesigner-mcp on PyPI</strong> — a second, unrelated package with the same name (v0.3.0, Oct 13 2026, MIT; Web Server DAT on port 9980, <span class="mono">uvx touchdesigner-mcp</span>). Do not confuse it with 8beeeaaat's server. <a href="https://pypi.org/project/touchdesigner-mcp/">PyPI</a></li>
    <li><strong>Cumulus</strong> — multi-camera people tracking with persistent cluster IDs and POP geometry masks; free tier, paid licence “planned at roughly $50–100 at launch” — pre-launch, unverified as a shipping price. <a href="https://cumulustracking.com/">cumulustracking.com</a></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="mcp" aria-labelledby="mcp-h">
  <h2 id="mcp-h">The MCP landscape</h2>
  <p class="sub">There is no single “the TouchDesigner MCP” in October 2026. A Deep Dive 2027 episode should compare these on tool count, transport, security model, and whether agent changes are undoable.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Maker</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>Price basis</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-h="Tool"><strong>TwoZero</strong></td><td data-h="Maker">404.zero + setupdesign</td><td data-h="Mechanism">Built-in MCP server (<span class="mono">localhost:40404/mcp</span>, key <span class="mono">twozero_td</span>) for Claude Code / Cursor / Codex, plus ZOP AI-model adapters</td><td data-h="Price">Plugin + MCP free forever; PRO $19/mo</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-h="Tool"><strong>Envoy</strong> (in Embody)</td><td data-h="Maker">Dylan Roscover</td><td data-h="Mechanism">Embedded MCP server — 52 tools on the current site; localhost:9870 in the older listing. Generates a CLAUDE.md for the agent; the TDXN text format gives readable project context</td><td data-h="Price">Free, open source</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-h="Tool"><strong>TDMCP</strong></td><td data-h="Maker">Derivative (official)</td><td data-h="Mechanism">MCP server inside TD on TD's bundled Python — 26 tools, docs-serving tools, agent Skills package; auth on by default, localhost-only, changes land in the undo stack</td><td data-h="Price">Free; Shared Use License</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-h="Tool"><strong>touchdesigner-mcp</strong></td><td data-h="Maker">8beeeaaat</td><td data-h="Mechanism">MCP ↔ WebServer DAT bridge; 14 tools; Claude Desktop extension</td><td data-h="Price">Free, MIT</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-h="Tool"><strong>tdmcp / MindDesigner</strong></td><td data-h="Maker">Pantani</td><td data-h="Mechanism">MCP server + in-TD bridge; 179 tools; embedded knowledge base of 629 operators and 68 Python classes</td><td data-h="Price">$0 listing</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-h="Tool"><strong>touchdesigner-mcp (PyPI)</strong></td><td data-h="Maker">Unnamed author</td><td data-h="Mechanism">MCP via <span class="mono">uvx</span>, Web Server DAT on port 9980</td><td data-h="Price">Free, MIT</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="sub" style="margin-top:12px">Not MCP, but part of the same shift: DotSimulate's <strong>LOPs</strong> put LLM / language operators inside TD, Mickey van Olst's <strong>AML</strong> includes a Local LLM operator on-device, and the <strong>TDXFam / FNSTools</strong> ecosystem is the infrastructure new agent-era tools ship on.</p>
</section>

<section id="diffusion" aria-labelledby="diff-h">
  <h2 id="diff-h">Real-time AI generation</h2>
  <p class="sub">The diffusion cluster, from the reference implementation to the native-operator challengers.</p>
  <ul class="plain" style="list-style:none;margin:0">
    <li><strong>StreamDiffusionTD — DotSimulate.</strong> The reference implementation: v0.4.1, SDXL-Turbo with ControlNet / IP-Adapter / FaceID / StreamV2V / live LoRA on TensorRT locally (Windows, NVIDIA 6 GB+ VRAM, 24 GB recommended, Python 3.11.9 exactly, CUDA 12.8), or via the Daydream cloud backend with no local GPU, including on Mac. <a href="https://daydream.live/streamdiffusiontd">Daydream page</a></li>
    <li><strong>ComfyTD — DotSimulate.</strong> A TOX to control ComfyUI workflows from inside a TD network. Distinct from ComfyUI-TD, a ComfyUI-side node for sending media back to TD — a name collision worth flagging in any catalogue.</li>
    <li><strong>SD TOP — Unveil Studio / Simo.</strong> Native-operator alternative with no Python or TensorRT model conversion. €15 for a 6-month licence via Lemon Squeezy; RTX 30/40/50 series.</li>
    <li><strong>TouchDiffusion — CtrlAltCtrl.</strong> Beta real-time diffusion tool announced on Patreon around October 2026; details unverified.</li>
    <li><strong>TwoZero ZOPs.</strong> Hosted generation as wired operators — 1,361 models at scan time, chat / image / video, cost shown before a run and failed generations not charged. Generation, but cloud-hosted rather than local diffusion.</li>
    <li><strong>Adjacent AI:</strong> AML's Diffusion and CoreML operators (on-device, macOS), Nurbs' depth + relight .tox (Metric3D v2 via ONNX), TwoZero's Depth AI and Background Removal rudiments, and TD-ML for training and inference on CHOP data.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="directories" aria-labelledby="dir-h">
  <h2 id="dir-h">Existing roundups &amp; directories</h2>
  <p class="sub">No single published directory found combines Patreon, Gumroad, and GitHub TouchDesigner tools with prices, licences, and TD-build requirements in one table — that gap is the niche this scan, and the 2027 series, can fill.</p>
  <ul class="plain" style="list-style:none;margin:0">
    <li><strong>Derivative Community</strong> — the canonical asset and tutorial feed where most of these tools are announced. Start with Function Store's curated article: <a href="https://derivative.ca/community-post/tools-you-didn%E2%80%99t-know-you-needed/72935">“Tools You Didn't Know You Needed”</a></li>
    <li><strong>allTD.org</strong> — tutorial aggregation, rebuilt as allTD v2 in April 2026: “5,000+ Tutorials: The largest collection of TouchDesigner content on the web (as of April 2026),” run by Jan Gryczan. <a href="https://alltd.org/">alltd.org</a></li>
    <li><strong>awesome-touchdesigner (GitHub)</strong> — curated list of resources, community projects, and plugins. <a href="https://github.com/monkeymonk/awesome-touchdesigner">github.com/monkeymonk/awesome-touchdesigner</a></li>
    <li><strong>Interactive &amp; Immersive HQ — “Top Community Tools for TouchDesigner”</strong> — editorial roundup covering Artio, SOP to SVG, Josef Pelz's Constraint Simulation, Warpa, and more. <a href="https://interactiveimmersive.io/blog/touchdesigner-lessons/top-community-tools-for-touchdesigner/">interactiveimmersive.io</a></li>
    <li><strong>Derivative — TouchDesigner Deep Dive 2020 resource list</strong> — the direct ancestor of the planned 2027 series, with its author / resource / link table. <a href="https://derivative.ca/community-post/touchdesigner-deep-dive-2020/71536">Deep Dive 2020</a></li>
    <li><strong>MusicHackspace “Custom Tools for TouchDesigner” meetup (Oct 2026)</strong> — a live roundup event with FNSTools, AVY, and MOPs toolmakers presenting. <a href="https://musichackspace.org/events/touchdesigner-meetup-custom-tools-october-2026">MusicHackspace</a></li>
    <li><strong>Storefronts as directories:</strong> Function Store's own site (86 searchable packages) and TwoZero's Hub / rudiments library act as de-facto directories for their ecosystems; MCP directories such as mcpservers.org, PulseMCP, and Glama now index the TD MCP servers.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

