<section id="method" aria-labelledby="method-h">
  <h2 id="method-h">Method &amp; caveats</h2>
  <div class="plain">
    <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px">
      <li style="margin:10px 0"><strong>Basis:</strong> web-index research as of October 24, 2026. Full primary pages were fetched through the index for TwoZero, Function Store / FNSTools, DotSimulate's StreamDiffusionTD docs, Embody, 404zero's TwoZero docs, and Derivative's TDMCP GitHub. Nothing here is labelled “verified live” — a separate live check could not resolve DNS for twozero.ai or functionstore.tools on Oct 24, which was a research-window failure, not evidence the sites are down.</li>
      <li style="margin:10px 0"><strong>Pricing rule:</strong> a price appears only where a public page exposed it. Patreon generally does not expose full tier tables to non-members, so most Patreon tier prices are unverified in this scan.</li>
      <li style="margin:10px 0"><strong>Conflicts carried, not resolved:</strong> TwoZero's minimum build is 2025.33230+ on twozero.ai and 2025.33070+ in the 404zero.com docs. Embody's is 2025.33230+ on the current site versus 2025.32280 on an earlier mirror. Envoy's tool count is 52 on the current site versus 45 in an MCP-repository listing. Resolve each by testing the current .tox.</li>
      <li style="margin:10px 0"><strong>Licences not found on public pages</strong> for SARV, T3D, RayTK (name), MediaPipe-TD (Torin's repo), Embody (specific name), AML, MOPs, GeoPix (specific name), Pantani's tdmcp, Dewpoint, Nurbs, AVY, and Warpa / SimpleMixer. Check each repo or maker before redistributing anything.</li>
      <li style="margin:10px 0"><strong>Spelling variants in sources:</strong> 404zero's Alexander Letcius (Derivative) vs Letsius (Interactive &amp; Immersive HQ). RayTK's author is “Tekt / t3kt” on primary sources; a full name on one course page was not corroborated and is not used here.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

